<title>NETHERLANDS: UNILEVER SET TO SELL UNIT TO ICI - PAPER.</title>
<headline>UNILEVER SET TO SELL UNIT TO ICI - PAPER.</headline>
<dateline>ROTTERDAM 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Unilever NV/Plc is set to announce the sale of its speciality chemicals business to Britain's Imperial Chemical Industries Plc , the European edition of the Wall Street Journal said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The paper, quoting sources &quot;familiar with the situation&quot;, said the firms were scheduled to announce a transaction on Wednesday, adding ICI may pay $8 billion for the chemicals unit.</p>
<p>Unilever's speciality chemicals business was put up for sale in February, prompting speculation that a number of firms, including ICI, might be interested. In April a British newspaper speculated ICI might pay four billion stg for the division.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
